```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures delivered == true; ensures present(session_id).
        // A violated ensures traps here rather than returning a bad confirmation.
        assert!(
            confirmation.delivered,
            "SendReply: channel did not confirm delivery"
        );
        assert!(
            !confirmation.session.is_empty(),
            "SendReply: channel returned an empty session id"
        );

        DeliveryConfirmation {
            session: confirmation.session,
            delivered: true,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I did not add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `response-channel`, and the enrichment call would send every reply's text to an external host on each invocation, which is outside the authority the graph declares. The platform approval needs to reach the graph definition first. Once the grant is in the graph, the fetch can be added without changing the output.

